{
  "bridge_text": "The memory of that mysterious fox is still fresh, so let us step back onto the threshold of the hollow tree where his quiet warning first echoed.",
  "resume_strategy": "restart",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "text": "Inside the hollow tree, the air felt cool and smelled of damp earth. A narrow curl of stairs wound downward into the dark. At the very top step sat an old grey fox wearing a patched green vest. This was Mosk. His voice sounded like dry leaves skittering on stone as he told Lina that the tree was not for visiting. He urged her to go home and forget the humming, but Lina stood firm, saying she could not possibly forget a song she had not yet heard."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s2"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "With the firefly resting on the moss, we return to the quiet song deep inside the hollow tree. Mosk’s heavy heart feels a little lighter just being near his old friend again.",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "Lina knelt beside the mossy bed and asked the firefly queen what she needed to feel strong once more. The queen whispered that a drop of warm milk and a kind word were all the medicine she had ever truly required. Mosk hurried to fetch the milk in a tiny silver thimble, laying his large, gentle paw beside hers as the queen’s soft glow began to steady and brighten."
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "text": "As the queen recovered, the humming inside the hollow tree shifted, transforming into a beautiful, ancient tune that Lina had never heard before. Mosk’s whiskers twitched with joy, and for the first time in many long years, he began to hum along with the melody, his voice blending perfectly with the magic of the woods."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s4"
}

{
